From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: use slab_build_skb() for kmalloc'd pool buffers

dpaa_bp_alloc_n_add_buffs() seeds a BMan pool's buffers via kmalloc()
and, when act_skb=true, wraps each buffer in an skb via
build_skb(ptr_buf, 0). Modern kernels (6.0+) added a WARN_ONCE in
__build_skb_around() that fires when frag_size == 0 — telling the caller
to use slab_build_skb() instead, which is the dedicated path for slab-
allocated buffers (it tracks the kmem_cache size and handles the
alignment-and-truesize accounting correctly).

cdx's IPsec output BMan pool seed (after A23) is the only consumer that
exercises act_skb=true on this code path, so the warning surfaces at
cdx module load. behaviorally the kernel auto-corrects via __slab_build_skb
after warning — so this patch is just removing the WARN noise, not
fixing a runtime regression. slab_build_skb() is a drop-in replacement
for build_skb(ptr, 0) on slab buffers.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
index ce91adf053a6..bb56ac6d22cb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@ int dpaa_bp_alloc_n_add_buffs(const struct dpa_bp *dpa_bp, uint32_t nbuffs, bool
 				 * We only need enough space to store a pointer, but allocate
 				 * an entire cacheline for performance reasons.
 				 */
-				skb = build_skb(ptr_buf, 0);
+				skb = slab_build_skb(ptr_buf);
 				if (unlikely(!skb)) {
 					pr_err("%s(%d) ii %d , buffs2fill %d build_skb failed \n",
 							__func__,__LINE__, ii, buffs2fill);
--
2.43.0
